Z||000000||mshill||12-09-1999||05:03 PM||||I have been bit hard by the Fiero bug. I purchased my 86SE in September and I am going<BR>to go pick up an 86GT in San Jose on the <BR>18th.  The guy has been trying to sell it <BR>on the alt.auto.fiero newsgroup for a couple<BR>of months and I just got the $$$ I needed in a bonus from work.  <P>My wife thinks I am nuts. My sons (13, 11, 9) think I'm great (I guess they think the Fieros are theirs in a few years).  And my neighbors are moving cause they think I'm white trash (four cars, two drivers...).<P>BTW, my 86SE, which I affectionately call "Swiss Cheese" sprung another coolant leak last night.  I should break down and just replace every part of the coolant system that isn't brand spanking new.  I have already replaced the radiator, front hoses, and the heater core.  I'm just waiting for the cross-over pipe to fall off the car.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-09-1999||06:22 PM||||Some people cant afford an expensive hobby like ours. People do say things that i own three cars.  Two of my cars run and one I'm restoring, 74 bug.  I know i have pride because i dont have to take my car in to get it fixed.  Also i dont look bad stalled on the side of the road, unless your ignition module goes out on you.  Saw a 95 my dodge stalled on the side of the road with the engine smoking, and i think he lost all his oil because my tires were spinning.  We cant be white trash because i never saw a fiero owner on Jerry Springer.||||reg||1
